                "id": "setting_header"
              },
              {
                "id": "setting_text"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "assumptions_text",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "content": "**Assumptions:** The luxury train is a fictional service, \"The Celestial Express,\" renowned for its opulent design and exclusive clientele, traveling through Europe in 1935. The murder takes place discreetly within one of the private compartments.",
            "style": "secondary"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "setting_divider",
          "type": "Divider"
        },
        {
          "id": "setting_header",
          "type": "Header",
          "properties": {
            "title": "Setting",
            "level": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "setting_text",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "content": "The year is 1935. The journey unfolds aboard \"The Celestial Express,\" a lavish, trans-European luxury train, as it makes its celebrated five-day voyage from the Gare de Lyon in Paris to the Sirkeci Terminal in Istanbul. The train is a moving palace of polished wood, brass, and velvet, filled with an eclectic mix of European aristocracy, industrialists, artists, and spies, all confined within its luxurious carriages as it speeds across picturesque landscapes and through bustling cities."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "crime_col",
          "type": "Column",
          "properties": {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "victim_header"
              },
              {
                "id": "victim_text"
              },
              {
                "id": "crime_divider"
              },
              {
                "id": "weapon_header"
              },
              {
                "id": "weapon_text"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "victim_header",
          "type": "Header",
          "properties": {
            "title": "The Victim: Baroness Eleanor Dubois",
            "level": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "victim_text",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "content": "A formidable and famously ruthless French industrialist, known for her sharp wit, scandalous past, and a reputation for crushing rivals without mercy. She is found dead in her lavish private compartment, appearing to have died peacefully in her sleep. However, a closer inspection reveals a tiny, almost invisible puncture mark on her neck."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "crime_divider",
          "type": "Divider"
        },
        {
          "id": "weapon_header",
          "type": "Header",
          "properties": {
            "title": "The Murder Weapon",
            "level": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "weapon_text",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "content": "A small, poisoned hatpin. The pin, intricately decorated with a faux pearl, was custom-made and coated with a fast-acting, undetectable neurotoxin. It was likely administered during a brief, close encounter, leaving minimal evidence."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "suspects_list",
          "type": "List",
          "properties": {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "suspect1_card"
              },
              {
                "id": "suspect2_card"
              },
              {
                "id": "suspect3_card"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "suspect1_card",
          "type": "Card",
          "properties": {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "suspect1_header"
              },
              {
                "id": "suspect1_text"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "suspect1_header",
          "type": "Header",
          "properties": {
            "title": "Monsieur Antoine Dubois",
            "subtitle": "The Estranged Nephew"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "suspect1_text",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "content": "**Motive: Financial Ruin and Revenge.** Antoine is the Baroness's estranged nephew, recently disinherited after his failing art gallery was refused a crucial loan by his aunt. He is desperate, facing bankruptcy, and believes the Baroness deliberately sabotaged his attempts to secure funding. He stands to inherit a substantial sum upon her death due to a clause in an older will."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "suspect2_card",
          "type": "Card",
          "properties": {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "suspect2_header"
              },
              {
                "id": "suspect2_text"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "suspect2_header",
          "type": "Header",
          "properties": {
            "title": "Lady Beatrice Finch",
            "subtitle": "The Demure Socialite"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "suspect2_text",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "content": "**Motive: Long-held Grudge and Social Retribution.** Lady Beatrice's prominent family suffered a devastating financial collapse years ago, directly attributable to a hostile takeover orchestrated by Baroness Dubois. Her family was publicly shamed and impoverished, and she has carried a quiet, simmering resentment."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "suspect3_card",
          "type": "Card",
          "properties": {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "suspect3_header"
              },
              {
                "id": "suspect3_text"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "suspect3_header",
          "type": "Header",
          "properties": {
            "title": "Dr. Alistair Reed",
            "subtitle": "The Renowned Archaeologist"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "suspect3_text",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "content": "**Motive: Professional Integrity and Protection of Legacy.** Dr. Reed is traveling with an invaluable ancient artifact that the Baroness had aggressively attempted to acquire through questionable means. Her tactics threatened to discredit Dr. Reed's reputation and research. He feared she would stop at nothing to possess it."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "twist_col",
          "type": "Column",
          "properties": {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "twist_header"
              },
              {
                "id": "twist_text"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "twist_header",
          "type": "Header",
          "properties": {
            "title": "The Plot Twist",
            "level": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "twist_text",
          "type": "Text",
          "properties": {
            "content": "The true killer is Lady Beatrice Finch, but her primary motive is not personal revenge. Lady Beatrice is an undercover agent for the British Secret Service. Baroness Dubois was secretly a key figure in an international espionage ring, planning to sell highly sensitive industrial and military secrets to a rival power in Istanbul. Lady Beatrice was assigned to eliminate the Baroness and retrieve crucial documents. Her family's historical grievance served as a perfect cover, diverting suspicion from her true mission. The poisoned hatpin was a specialized tool developed by the Secret Service for discreet assassinations. The other suspects' motives were elaborate red herrings, carefully placed or exploited by Lady Beatrice to further obscure her real objective."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
]
